          "type": "output_text",
          "text": "The review identified one relevant cost event for **work order MO-25-09-1070** (work order ID **WO-2025-09-004**):\n\n- **Source transaction:** `TXN-ISSUE-250930-1070` — component-issue `INPUT`\n- **Amount:** **$318,250.75** (31,825,075 cents)\n- **Event created:** `2025-09-30T20:25:00`\n- **September period entered Pending Close:** `2025-09-30T18:00:00`\n- **Time after Pending Close:** **145 minutes** (2 hours 25 minutes)\n- **Recorded accounting status:** `POSTED`\n\n**Conclusion:** The `POSTED` status is **not consistent** with the supplied Oracle Cost Management 26B Pending Close policy. It says transactions created after the Pending Close date are not processed, apart from specified exceptions such as revenue lines, COGS recognition, and manual cost adjustments. This component issue is not one of those exceptions.\n\nThe review was read-only; no database records were changed.",
